    "text": "Let \\(A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ k & 1 & k \\\\ 3 & k & 2 \\end{bmatrix}\\). Find the \\((2, 1)\\)-entry of the inverse matrix \\(A^{-1}\\).",
